<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1941</h1><p class="ref-lede">1941 in world history: 63 events, 6 births, 19 deaths, 2 works, 10 states founded and 7 that came to an end. 720 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1937">1937</a><a href="/years/1938">1938</a><a href="/years/1939">1939</a><a href="/years/1940">1940</a><a href="/years/1941" aria-current="page">1941</a><a href="/years/1942">1942</a><a href="/years/1943">1943</a><a href="/years/1944">1944</a><a href="/years/1945">1945</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-6">6 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt sets out the 'Four Freedoms'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In his State of the Union address, Franklin Roosevelt named freedom of speech, freedom of worship, freedom from want and freedom from fear as universal rights. The speech shaped Allied war aims and the UN.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-11">11 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt signs the Lend-Lease Act</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The act allowed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> to lend or lease war supplies to nations whose defence was vital to America. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> received some 50 billion dollars of aid.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lend-lease">Lend-Lease</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-28">28 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Virginia Woolf drowns herself in the River Ouse</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Fearing a return of mental illness, the novelist filled her pockets with stones and walked into the river near her Sussex home. Her novels include 'Mrs Dalloway' and 'To the Lighthouse'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-29">29 March</a> · Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cape-matapan">Battle of Cape Matapan</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Cape Matapan was a naval battle fought on 27–29 March 1941 off the south-western coast of the Peloponnese, Greece, between the British Mediterranean Fleet under Admiral Andrew Cunningham and the Italian navy.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-24">24 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Bismarck sinks HMS Hood in the Denmark Strait</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A shell from the German battleship detonated Hood's magazine, and she sank in minutes; only three of her 1,418 crew survived. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> hunted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bismarck-battleship">Bismarck</a> down three days later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-27">27 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Royal Navy sinks the battleship Bismarck</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Crippled by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torpedo">torpedo</a> hit to her rudder, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bismarck-battleship">Bismarck</a> was pounded by British battleships and sank in the Atlantic. Only about 114 of her crew of over 2,000 survived.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/black-sea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-22">22 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germany invades the Soviet Union</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/operation-barbarossa">Operation Barbarossa</a> sent some three million <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> troops across a front from the Baltic to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. The war in the east became the largest and deadliest land conflict in history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-11">11 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ground is broken for the Pentagon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Construction began on the Pentagon in Arlington, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, to house the War <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a>. Finished in just 16 months, it remains one of the world's largest office buildings.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-7">7 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Japan attacks Pearl Harbor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese carrier aircraft struck the US Pacific Fleet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>, killing more than 2,400 Americans and sinking or damaging 19 ships. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> entered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-8">8 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The United States and Britain declare war on Japan</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Franklin Roosevelt asked Congress to declare war, calling 7 December 'a date which will live in infamy'. Congress agreed within the hour, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> also declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-11">11 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germany and Italy declare war on the United States</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Four days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a>, Hitler and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> declared war on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. The decision brought American power fully into the war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/operation-barbarossa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-barbarossa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/operation-barbarossa">Operation Barbarossa</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Operation Barbarossa was the German invasion of the Soviet Union, launched on 22 June 1941 by some three million German troops with Romanian, Finnish and other allied forces.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rumbula-massacre" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rumbula-massacre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/rumbula-massacre">Rumbula massacre</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Rumbula massacre was the killing of about 25,000 Jews in Rumbula forest near Riga on 30 November and 8 December 1941.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-soviet-invasion-of-iran" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-soviet-invasion-of-iran.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/anglo-soviet-invasion-of-iran">Anglo-Soviet invasion of Iran</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Anglo-Soviet invasion of Iran took place in August and September 1941, when British and Soviet forces occupied the country to secure its oilfields and a supply route to the Soviet Union during the Second World War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/farhud" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/farhud.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/farhud">Farhud</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Farhud was a violent pogrom against the Jews of Baghdad on 1–2 June 1941, in the power vacuum after the fall of Rashid Ali's pro-Axis government and before British troops entered the city.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ko-chang">Battle of Ko Chang</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Ko Chang was a naval engagement fought on 17 January 1941 off the island of Ko Chang in the Gulf of Thailand, during the Franco-Thai War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-saio" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-saio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-saio">Battle of Saïo</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Saïo was fought in south-western Ethiopia in June and July 1941, during the East African campaign of the Second World War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-zarumilla" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-zarumilla.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-zarumilla">Battle of Zarumilla</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Zarumilla was fought in July 1941 near the Zarumilla River on the border between Ecuador and Peru.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-iraqi-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-iraqi-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/anglo-iraqi-war">Anglo-Iraqi War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Anglo-Iraqi War was a British campaign in May 1941 against the government of Rashid Ali al-Gaylani, which had seized power in Iraq in a pro-Axis coup in April.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-keren" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-keren.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-keren">Battle of Keren</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Keren was fought from February to March 1941 in the mountains around the town of Keren in Eritrea, between Italian forces and British and Indian troops.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/kragujevac-massacre" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kragujevac-massacre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/kragujevac-massacre">Kragujevac massacre</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Kragujevac massacre was the mass shooting of some 2,800 men and boys, including schoolboys, by German troops in the Serbian town of Kragujevac in October 1941.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/ecuadorian-peruvian-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ecuadorian-peruvian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/ecuadorian-peruvian-war">Ecuadorian–Peruvian War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Ecuadorian–Peruvian War was a border war fought in July 1941 between Ecuador and Peru over disputed Amazonian and coastal territory.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Crisis</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/us-oil-embargo-against-japan">US oil embargo against Japan</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The US oil embargo against Japan was the cutting off of American oil exports to Japan in 1941, imposed in response to Japanese expansion in Indochina.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaties-of-rome-1941">Treaties of Rome (1941)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaties of Rome were agreements signed on 18 May 1941 between Fascist Italy and the newly created Independent State of Croatia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/liberation-of-ethiopia-1941">Liberation of Ethiopia (1941)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The liberation of Ethiopia in 1941 was the defeat of Italian occupation forces by British and Commonwealth troops working with Ethiopian patriots during the Second World War.</p></div></li></ol></section>
